---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lastUpdated = '2026-11-15';
// Match the build-time vendor switches in Layout.astro and posthog.astro.
const hasPostHog = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN && import.meta.env.PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST);
const hasClarity = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID);
const hasMetaPixel = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID);
---
<style>
  /* Anyone linking directly to #testflight (historical TestFlight section)
     lands mid-list; mark which bullet they landed on. */
  li:target { border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 12px; margin-left: -14px; }
</style>
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — health4.ai"
  description="How health4.ai handles your Apple Health data."
>
  <nav class="flex items-center justify-between px-6 py-5 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <a href="/" class="text-green-400 font-bold text-lg tracking-tight hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">health4.ai</a>
  </nav>

  <main class="px-6 py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-invert prose-sm">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs mb-10">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      health4.ai ("we", "us") provides an iOS app and MCP server that facilitate the transfer of Apple HealthKit data to a destination <em>you configure and control</em>: a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive or a Postgres/Supabase database. We do not operate a shared health-data backend or collect, store, or have access to your health data. This policy explains what limited data we do collect and your rights.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">1. What data we collect</h2>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Health data: we do not collect it.</strong> HealthKit metrics you authorize flow directly from your device to a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive (if you choose Save to Google Sheets; see section 4) or to a Supabase project you create and own. health4.ai never receives, stores, or has access to your health data. A cloud AI provider you separately connect to may process data you choose to send to it.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Bike on your network (optional, version 1.0.6 and later).</strong> If you turn this on, the app reads finished rides from a ride server on your own home Wi-Fi, at a local address you enter, and saves each ride to the Apple Health app on your iPhone as an indoor cycling workout with active energy, cycling distance, power, cadence and, if you allow it, heart rate. This needs two permissions you can refuse or withdraw at any time: writing those types to Health, and iOS Local Network access. The app only connects to local network addresses for this feature and never to any internet server. Nothing is sent to health4.ai, and nothing is written to Health unless you turn the feature on. Rides you import stay in Health if you turn it off or erase the app's data; you can delete them in the Health app.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Account data</strong>: before launch, we collected email addresses from pre-launch waitlist sign-ups to notify people when the app shipped and, for those who opted in, to send a TestFlight beta invitation. The app is now live on the App Store and we no longer collect waitlist emails.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Website usage data</strong>: the website tools enabled for this build are described in section 8. These are separate from the iOS app's HealthKit sync. Do not send health records, passwords or database credentials in a support message.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">2. How we use it</h2>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li>Previously, to notify pre-launch waitlist sign-ups when the app shipped on the App Store. That notification has gone out and this collection is closed.</li>
        <li id="testflight" class="scroll-mt-6"><strong class="text-neutral-200">TestFlight invitations (historical): opt-in, and shared with Apple.</strong> During the pre-launch beta, if you ticked the TestFlight box when joining the waitlist, we passed your email address to Apple's App Store Connect so Apple could send you a beta invitation. Apple sent that email, not us. Anyone with administrator access to our App Store Connect account could see the addresses of enrolled testers. If you were a tester, ask us at any time to remove you.</li>
        <li>To understand website use and improve reliability, using the tools described in section 8.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm mt-3">
        We do not sell personal data. We do not use health data for advertising. The app's health-data sync sends records directly to the destination you configure, rather than through a health4.ai-operated backend. Keep your device, destination credentials and sharing settings secure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">3. Where data is stored</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Your health data lives in the destination <em>you</em> choose: a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive (see section 4), or a Supabase project you create and own. You control the destination credentials and sharing settings. People or services you authorize, and the destination provider, may be able to access the data under those settings. We do not receive a copy through the sync service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="google" class="mb-8 scroll-mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">4. Google Sheets destination</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
        health4.ai offers a destination, "Save to Google Sheets", that writes your health summaries into a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive instead of a database. It is available in version 1.0.1 of the app and later. If you never connect a Google account, none of this section applies and we receive nothing from Google.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">What Google data the app accesses.</strong> When you choose this destination, the app asks you to sign in to Google on your device and requests a single permission (OAuth scope): <code class="break-all">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file</code>. This scope limits the app to files it creates itself. health4.ai cannot see, list, or open any other file in your Google Drive, and it does not request your name, email address, contacts, calendar, or Gmail.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">How it is used.</strong> The app creates one spreadsheet in your Drive and writes daily health summaries and workout rows into it, plus sleep stage rows if you turn them on (version 1.0.4 and later), directly from your iPhone to Google's Sheets API. That is the only purpose.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">How it is stored.</strong> The Google sign-in token (a refresh token) is stored in the iOS Keychain on your device. It never leaves your phone except to talk to Google. The health rows live in your Google Drive, under your Google account and Google's own security.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">How it is shared.</strong> It is not shared. No Google user data or health data is sent to health4.ai or to any server we operate. We do not sell it, use it for advertising, or transfer it to anyone else, and no human at health4.ai reads it, because we never receive it. The app talks to Google directly and to no one else on this path.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Revoke access.</strong> In the app, disconnect Google Sheets; the app revokes its token with Google and forgets it. You can also remove access at any time in your Google Account under Security → Third-party connections, or at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. Either way, sync stops.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Delete.</strong> Disconnecting does not delete the spreadsheet; it is your file, and you can delete it in Google Drive whenever you like. Erasing the app's data removes the stored sign-in token from your device's Keychain. Because we hold none of this data, there is nothing on our side to delete.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4" id="google-limited-use">
        <strong class="text-neutral-200">Google API Services User Data Policy.</strong> health4ai's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy#additional_requirements_for_specific_api_scopes" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Limited Use requirements</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">5. HIPAA</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        health4.ai is a personal tool for moving health data to a destination you control, not a service offered to handle protected health information on behalf of a healthcare provider or health plan. HIPAA status depends on the actual relationship and activities, not simply whether a Business Associate Agreement has been signed. Do not assume that using the app makes your destination or an AI service HIPAA-compliant.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">6. Your rights</h2>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Health data control</strong>: your health data is in your Google Sheet or your database. You can delete it directly at any time, with no request to us required.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Data we hold</strong>: contact us to request access, correction or deletion of historical waitlist, tester or support records. We may verify the request and will respond within the applicable legal deadline. We explain any information retained for a legal or security reason; backup copies may remain until they expire.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Revoke HealthKit access</strong>: stop syncing at any time in iPhone Settings → Privacy & Security → Health → health4.ai. No data is deleted from your Google Sheet or database automatically; you remain in full control.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Additional rights</strong>: depending on your location and the law that applies, you may have rights to export information, object to processing, or opt out of advertising-related sharing. Contact us to make a request or ask us to review a decision. We do not penalize you for exercising applicable privacy rights.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">7. Breach notification</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The sync architecture does not route your health records through a health4.ai-operated backend. This reduces the information we hold, but it is not a guarantee against security incidents affecting the app, website, support records, your device or your chosen destination. If we discover an incident, we assess its scope and provide notifications required by applicable law within the applicable deadlines.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">8. Analytics & cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The website is hosted by Cloudflare, which processes technical request information such as
        IP addresses to deliver and protect the site. The following optional integrations reflect
        this website build's configuration; they are website tools, not part of the HealthKit sync.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0 mt-3">
        {hasPostHog && <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">PostHog (US-hosted)</strong> receives website page views and interactions and uses a browser identifier in local storage. Its recording configuration masks form inputs; recorded page content and browser identifiers should not be treated as anonymous.</li>}
        {hasClarity && <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Microsoft Clarity</strong> receives website interaction and recording data under Microsoft's privacy policy.</li>}
        {hasMetaPixel && <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Meta Pixel</strong> receives page visits and connection information for advertising measurement. Meta may associate visits with its own identifiers. This may count as sharing or targeted advertising under applicable privacy laws.</li>}
        {!hasPostHog && !hasClarity && !hasMetaPixel && <li>No optional PostHog, Microsoft Clarity or Meta Pixel integration is enabled in this website build.</li>}
      </ul>
      {(hasPostHog || hasClarity || hasMetaPixel) && <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3">
        These configured tools currently load on production website visits without an on-site consent
        selector. You can use your browser's blocking controls and contact us about privacy choices;
        we do not currently claim that this website automatically honors Global Privacy Control.
      </p>}
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3">
        We do not send HealthKit records to these website tools. We have not set a uniform automatic
        deletion interval across historical mailing-list records, support messages and provider
        analytics. Contact us about the records we hold and their deletion. Changing browser storage
        does not delete information already received by a provider.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        We will update the "Last updated" date when this policy changes. For material changes we provide any notice and obtain any consent required by applicable law before applying the change.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">10. Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Questions or data requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@health4.ai" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">privacy@health4.ai</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-neutral-800/60 px-6 py-8 mt-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 text-neutral-600 text-xs">
      <span>© 2026 health4.ai · Not a medical device</span>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
        <a href="/about/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">About</a>
        <a href="/contact/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Contact</a>
        <a href="/privacy/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/terms/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Terms</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/jefflitt1/health4ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
